.TH QUOTA-STATUS 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quota-status \- print Linux quota activation status without modifying it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quota-status
.RB ( --all " | " --filesystem " MOUNTPOINT )"
.br
.B quota-status
.RB [ --help " | " --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the native Linux quotaon program with
.B -p
(print-only status). The standard output of the native program is forwarded unchanged. This utility does not enable or disable quota accounting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --all
Execute quotaon -p -a.
.TP
.B --filesystem MOUNTPOINT
Execute quotaon -p MOUNTPOINT using a canonical absolute directory path.
.TP
.BR --help , " --version"
Show usage or version.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Linux, Perl 5 and the operating-system's quotaon command with -p support. Unavailable commands or unsupported options produce an error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if quotaon exited normally; 2 for invalid input; 3 for unsupported platforms or prerequisite/native-command failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quotaon (8),
.BR quota-report (1),
.BR quota-set (8)
